id: pm-oh24c5
title: "pm validate reports stored identities that carry URL userinfo, with a rewrite remediation"
description: "Follow-up to pm-gh1707. New writes strip URL userinfo from author, assignee and claim principal, and refusals and claim envelopes redact a stored one, but a holder written by an older version stays in the item file and in full item reads (pm get, list, claim with full changed fields) as stored. Nothing tells a maintainer that such a record exists. pm validate (and pm health) should report each item whose author, assignee or claim_principal carries URL userinfo, by item id and field only, never the value, with the remediation pm update <id> --assignee <name> or a fresh claim, so a tracker can be cleaned deliberately instead of by accident."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 3
tags[5]: agent-ux,privacy,redaction,security,validate
created_at: "2026-11-12T08:23:44.023Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-13T03:07:36.588Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "pm validate and pm health report items whose author, assignee or claim_principal carries URL userinfo, naming the item id and field but never the value; Each finding carries the rewrite remediation; A tracker without such records reports nothing"
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: A maintainer learns about legacy credential-bearing identities and can rewrite them
actual_result: Legacy identities with URL userinfo are invisible until echoed in full item reads
